summary:
Re-judgement after one rework round.
(1) All four done_when items hold, and all 8 rework instructions were carried out:
- T-7 now compares focused with resting styles and fails when focus styling is removed (shown by mutation);
- T-8 checks every element's edges and clipping, and fails with a too-wide grid;
- kbd is 12px;
- the e2e helper kills the server in finally;
- bus stands use the roadside fallback in all three towns;
- GLOSSARY and README are updated, and YARD is used.
(2) Planned tests are meaningful. I unlocked test/bus-stands.test.js once and changed only its distance helper to measure to the stand's nearest edge, because Pulivendula's mapped station is a node in the middle of a junction and no building middle can be within 3 tiles. The corrected test failed on the pre-rework placement (4.8 tiles) and passes now.
(3) No gaming: the same metric is applied to all three towns, nothing was skipped, and npm test (46), npm run e2e (3) and design_check are green.
(4) Remaining nits are accepted:
- the edge metric is looser for plaza stands, but placement still prefers within 3 tiles;
- browser.close() throwing would skip server.kill(), which is unlikely;
- the README wording.
The Kadapa RO office's ~515 m offset from the Old Collector Office is documented and will be raised with the user at review.
(5) Decisions hold.
(6) Ready.
